// src/app/data/gaming-servers-faqs.data.ts
var GAMING_FAQS = [
  [
    "What Is A Dedicated Game Server?",
    "A dedicated game server is a physical machine that hosts online multiplayer games. It manages all game data and player traffic centrally and stays online 24/7, independent of any player's device \u2014 unlike peer-to-peer hosting."
  ],
  [
    "Why Choose XcellHost For Game Servers?",
    "Servers in Mumbai and Pune give low ping to players across India, with high-clock CPUs, NVMe storage, full root access, always-on DDoS protection, INR billing and engineers available 24\xD77."
  ],
  [
    "How Is It Better Than Peer-To-Peer Hosting?",
    "There's no host advantage, the session doesn't end when one player leaves, anti-cheat is stronger, and you control every setting and who can join."
  ],
  [
    "How Do I Set Up My Game Server?",
    "Choose a configuration, location and operating system. We provision the server and send root access, then you install your game or a game panel such as Pterodactyl \u2014 or ask us to set it up."
  ],
  [
    "Can I Install Mods And Plugins?",
    "Yes. Full root access lets you upload custom files, run modded builds and manage modpacks \u2014 Forge or Fabric for Minecraft, Oxide for Rust and so on."
  ],
  [
    "How Does DDoS Protection Work?",
    "Traffic is filtered at the network edge in real time, so attack traffic is dropped while genuine player connections continue."
  ],
  [
    "What Performance Can I Expect?",
    "Dedicated hardware gives steadier tick rates, lower latency, faster loading from NVMe and room for mods \u2014 with no other tenants sharing your CPU."
  ],
  [
    "How Many Players Can A Server Handle?",
    "It depends on the game and mods. High-clock CPUs, plenty of RAM and fast ports support anything from a small group to large communities \u2014 tell us the game and player count and we'll size it."
  ]
];

