// src/app/data/performance-cloud-faqs.data.ts
var PERFORMANCE_CLOUD_FAQS = [
  ["What is XcellHost Performance Cloud?", "XcellHost Performance Cloud is a range of NVMe-backed cloud servers hosted in India, offered in five instance families \u2014 Shared CPU, Standard dedicated vCPU, CPU-Optimised, Memory-Optimised and High-IOPS storage \u2014 so each workload gets the right balance of cores, memory and disk. Servers launch in minutes, run Windows or Linux, bill hourly or monthly in INR with a GST invoice, and are supported 24\xD77 by XcellHost engineers. Plans start from \u20B9399 per month."],
  ["What is the difference between Shared CPU and Dedicated vCPU?", "Shared CPU instances draw from a pool of cores that is fairly scheduled between tenants \u2014 excellent value for websites, staging and bursty workloads. Dedicated vCPU (Standard, CPU-Optimised, Memory-Optimised and High-IOPS) reserves each vCPU for you alone, so performance stays consistent under sustained load. Use shared for light or spiky work, dedicated for anything in production that customers or staff depend on."],
  ["Which instance family should I choose?", "Start from the bottleneck. Mostly idle or bursty: Shared. General production app: Standard. CPU pinned at 100% for long periods: CPU-Optimised. Database or cache that wants more RAM: Memory-Optimised. Disk queue always busy: High-IOPS. If you're unsure, tell us what you run and we'll size it free."],
  ["Which operating systems are supported?", "Windows Server 2019, 2022 and 2025, plus Ubuntu, Debian, AlmaLinux, Rocky Linux, CentOS Stream and FreeBSD. Red Hat Enterprise Linux is available on a bring-your-own-licence basis, and you can upload a custom ISO."],
  ["Is Windows licensing included?", "Windows Server licensing is available as a monthly add-on priced per two vCPUs, so you never buy a perpetual licence up front. Linux distributions carry no licence charge."],
  ["What storage do the servers use?", "Every plan runs on enterprise NVMe SSD \u2014 including the entry Shared plan. High-IOPS instances add large local NVMe for write-heavy workloads, and you can attach extra block storage volumes to any server."],
  ["Can I resize a server later?", "Yes. You can add vCPU, memory or storage from the console without rebuilding the server; a CPU or RAM change needs a brief reboot. You can also move between instance families as the workload changes."],
  ["How does billing work \u2014 hourly or monthly?", "Both. Pay hourly to test or for short-lived environments, or take a monthly plan. Committing to 3, 6 or 12 months saves 5%, 7.5% or 10%. Every invoice is in INR with GST, so you can claim input tax credit."],
  ["Are there charges for bandwidth or data transfer?", "Each plan includes a generous monthly bandwidth allowance, and we don't bill per GB of outbound traffic within it. If you consistently exceed it, we'll talk to you about a larger allocation before any overage appears."],
  ["Where are the servers hosted, and does my data stay in India?", "Servers run in Indian data centres and your data stays in India unless you choose otherwise \u2014 useful for DPDP Act obligations and for low latency to Indian users."],
  ["How secure is XcellHost Performance Cloud?", "Tenants are isolated at the hypervisor, every server gets a stateful virtual firewall and upstream anti-DDoS, and our operations are ISO 27001 certified with 24\xD77 NOC and SOC oversight. Acronis Cyber Protect adds backup and anti-malware if you want it."],
  ["What uptime do you guarantee?", "A 99.95% uptime SLA on the platform, backed by redundant power, cooling, network and host hardware, with service credits if we miss it."],
  ["Do you help with migration?", "Yes, and it's free when you move to XcellHost. We assess the current setup, write a cut-over plan, rehearse it on a copy, and switch over out of hours so users barely notice."],
  ["Can I run Docker and Kubernetes?", "Yes. Deploy Docker hosts or a K3s cluster from the one-click catalogue, connect nodes over private networking, and put a load balancer in front."],
  ["Can I try it before committing?", "Yes \u2014 start on hourly billing with no lock-in, prove the workload, and move to a monthly or term plan once you're happy. Ask us about a guided proof-of-concept for larger migrations."],
  ["What support do I get?", "24\xD77 support by phone, WhatsApp and ticket from XcellHost engineers in Mumbai, in English and Hindi. It's included with every plan \u2014 there's no paid tier to unlock a human."]
];

// src/app/data/edr-seo.data.ts
var ACRONIS_EDR_FAQS = [
  [
    "How much does managed EDR cost per endpoint in India?",
    "Acronis Advanced Endpoint Security (EDR) starts at \u20B9999 per user per year, excluding GST. The published one-, two- and three-year plans currently use the same annual per-user rate; confirm endpoint quantities and any managed-service scope before ordering."
  ],
  [
    "Which operating systems does Acronis EDR support?",
    "Acronis EDR supports Windows, macOS and selected Linux workloads. Feature depth and supported versions differ by operating system, so XcellHost validates every device type and OS version during scoping before rollout."
  ],
  [
    "How long does EDR deployment take?",
    "A representative pilot can usually begin once tenant access, endpoint inventory and policies are approved. Estate-wide timing depends on device count, software-distribution tools, network access and change windows; XcellHost confirms a deployment plan during onboarding."
  ],
  [
    "Does EDR replace antivirus?",
    "It can replace a standalone antivirus when the selected protection plan enables Acronis anti-malware and endpoint-protection controls. EDR adds continuous telemetry, investigation and response; XcellHost checks coexistence and removes conflicting endpoint agents safely."
  ],
  [
    "Can Acronis EDR roll back ransomware changes?",
    "On supported workloads and configurations, Acronis can stop malicious activity and use local cache or integrated backup data for recovery. Rollback and remediation capabilities vary by operating system, licence and backup configuration, so they are verified during solution design."
  ],
  [
    "Who monitors and responds to EDR alerts?",
    "XcellHost can provide managed monitoring and incident assistance, with 24\xD77 emergency support for active security incidents. The published SLA targets a 15-minute response for P1 incidents and two hours for initial containment; customer cooperation and environment access remain required."
  ],
  [
    "Does managed EDR help with CERT-In reporting and DPDPA readiness?",
    "EDR telemetry, alert timelines and incident evidence can help an organisation assess and document an incident. This supports, but does not itself guarantee, compliance with CERT-In reporting or DPDPA security and breach-notification duties; the customer remains responsible for legal assessment and reporting."
  ],
  [
    "Is Acronis endpoint protection independently tested?",
    "Yes. AV-TEST publishes independent business endpoint-protection results for Acronis Cyber Protect. Buyers should review the current tested version, operating system and individual protection, performance and usability scores before treating a result as applicable to their deployment."
  ]
];
var SCRUTINY_EDR_FAQS = [
  [
    "How is Scrutiny EDR priced?",
    "Scrutiny EDR is quoted for the number and type of protected endpoints, deployment model and monitoring scope. XcellHost provides INR billing with GST and separates licence, implementation and managed-service requirements in the proposal."
  ],
  [
    "Which operating systems does Scrutiny EDR support?",
    "Scrutiny EDR is designed for Windows, macOS and Linux endpoints. Supported versions and response controls can differ by platform, so XcellHost validates the exact operating-system inventory before a pilot or production rollout."
  ],
  [
    "How long does Scrutiny EDR deployment take?",
    "Deployment starts with a representative pilot, policy tuning and alert validation. The full timeline depends on endpoint count, network reachability, software-distribution tooling and change windows; XcellHost confirms milestones after discovery."
  ],
  [
    "Does Scrutiny EDR replace antivirus?",
    "EDR and antivirus solve different layers of the problem. Scrutiny adds continuous endpoint visibility, behavioural detection, investigation and response. Whether an existing antivirus remains, is integrated or is replaced is decided during compatibility and policy review."
  ],
  [
    "Can Scrutiny EDR recover files after ransomware?",
    "Scrutiny can detect ransomware behaviour and provide containment and remediation actions. File or system recovery depends on the affected platform and a separate, tested backup strategy; EDR should not be treated as a substitute for backup."
  ],
  [
    "Who monitors Scrutiny EDR alerts?",
    "Your security team can operate the platform, or XcellHost can provide managed 24\xD77 monitoring, triage, incident coordination and reporting from its Mumbai SOC. Responsibilities and response targets are documented in the selected service agreement."
  ],
  [
    "Does Scrutiny EDR help with CERT-In reporting and DPDPA readiness?",
    "Endpoint timelines, audit trails and incident evidence can support investigation and reporting workflows. They do not automatically make an organisation compliant; the customer remains responsible for deciding whether an event is reportable and for meeting applicable legal duties."
  ],
  [
    "Can we test Scrutiny EDR before a full rollout?",
    "Yes. XcellHost can scope a representative pilot to validate agent compatibility, detections, response permissions, alert routing and operational ownership before broad deployment."
  ]
];

// src/app/data/cloud-drive-seo.data.ts
var CLOUD_DRIVE_SEO_FAQS = [
  [
    "What is XcellHost Cloud Drive?",
    "XcellHost Cloud Drive is a business file-storage, sync and collaboration service with centrally managed users, team folders, version history and controlled external sharing. It is designed for organisations that need company-managed storage instead of files scattered across personal drives, email and messaging apps."
  ],
  [
    "How much does XcellHost Cloud Drive cost?",
    "Plans start at \u20B92,499 per customer per month for 250 GB of pooled storage and unlimited users. Published prices exclude GST. Larger plans provide 500 GB, 1 TB, 2 TB or 5 TB, with discounted three-month, six-month and annual billing."
  ],
  [
    "How much storage does each Cloud Drive user receive?",
    "Storage is pooled for the customer rather than assigned as a fixed allowance per user. The organisation chooses a 250 GB to 5 TB plan and can create unlimited users, while administrators control folders, permissions and storage use."
  ],
  [
    "Where is Cloud Drive data stored?",
    "The standard XcellHost Cloud Drive offer stores customer data in Indian data centres. Confirm the selected region, backup arrangement and any sector-specific residency requirement in the service order before activation."
  ],
  [
    "How is Cloud Drive data encrypted?",
    "The published File Cloud SLA specifies AES-256 encryption for data at rest and TLS 1.2 or 1.3 for data in transit. It also lists role-based access, multi-factor authentication, audit logging and password- or expiry-protected sharing."
  ],
  [
    "Does Cloud Drive support DPDPA compliance?",
    "Indian data residency, access controls, audit logs and controlled sharing can support an organisation\u2019s DPDPA security and governance measures. No storage product guarantees compliance by itself; customers must configure access, retention and lawful processing for their own obligations."
  ],
  [
    "How is XcellHost Cloud Drive different from Google Drive or OneDrive?",
    "Cloud Drive provides pooled organisation-level storage, unlimited users on the published plans, Indian data residency and local XcellHost migration and support. Google Drive and OneDrive are tightly integrated with their respective productivity suites and are commonly licensed per user."
  ],
  [
    "Can XcellHost migrate files from a server, Google Drive, OneDrive or Dropbox?",
    "Yes. XcellHost can scope migration from file servers and common cloud-drive platforms, including folder structure, permissions and cutover planning. Timing and migration method depend on data volume, source-platform access, internet bandwidth and the condition of the source data."
  ]
];

