var GOVERNANCE_FAQS = [["I already have P2. What does ID Governance add?", "P2 gives you the core of access reviews, entitlement management and PIM. The add-on adds lifecycle workflows for joiners, movers and leavers, auto-assignment of access packages by attributes, ML-assisted review recommendations, inactive-user and peer-outlier insights, and on-premises and SAP provisioning connectors."], ["Who needs a licence \u2014 just employees?", "Every user who is governed \u2014 in scope of a workflow, an access package or a review \u2014 needs one, and so do the reviewers and approvers who take part. Guest users are handled differently by Microsoft, based on monthly active users; we'll size that with you."], ["Which HR systems can drive provisioning?", "Workday and SAP SuccessFactors have built-in connectors. Other HR systems \u2014 including Indian HRMS and payroll platforms \u2014 can push hires, changes and exits through API-driven provisioning, often from a scheduled CSV export. We set up and test the mapping with you."], ["How quickly is a leaver's access removed?", "A leaver workflow can run on the last working day, or immediately when HR records an exit. It disables the account, revokes sessions, removes groups and access packages and triggers deprovisioning in connected apps \u2014 typically completing within minutes of the trigger."], ["How do ML-assisted access-review suggestions work?", "For each decision, the reviewer sees a recommendation based on signals such as sign-in inactivity and whether the person's access is unusual compared with their peers. Reviewers can accept recommendations in bulk and focus on the exceptions. The final decision always stays with the reviewer."], ["Will it help with DPDP Act and RBI audits?", "It helps you meet access-control expectations \u2014 least-privilege access, periodic user-access reviews, privileged-access controls and audit trails \u2014 and produces reports your auditors can use. Compliance itself also depends on your policies and processes, which we can review with you."], ["Can I pay monthly?", "Yes \u2014 \u20B9528 per user per month, or \u20B96,125 per user for the year paid upfront. Both are below Microsoft's list price and exclude 18% GST. Microsoft licences carry an annual commitment either way; you can add users at any time."], ["Is governing AI agents available today?", "Governance of AI agent identities \u2014 sponsors, blueprints, access packages and reviews for agents \u2014 is in preview, so features and terms can change before general availability. We'll tell you what's ready for production when we plan your rollout."], ["How long does a rollout take?", "A typical first phase \u2014 HR connector, joiner and leaver workflows, and one access review \u2014 runs over a few weeks, starting with a pilot department. Larger estates with SAP or on-premises connectors take longer; we'll give you a plan after the tenant review."]];

