<section class="sec alt" id="india">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sh rv"><span class="eyebrow">For regulated Indian businesses</span><h2>Controls auditors <span class="acc">ask to see.</span></h2><p>Indian regulators keep returning to the same three themes: strong authentication, tight control of privileged accounts and regular access reviews. P2 helps you meet them \u2014 and produces the evidence.</p></div>
    <div class="g4">
      <div class="card reg rv"><div class="ico n"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18" rx="1"></rect><path d="M9 7h.01M15 7h.01M9 11h.01M15 11h.01M9 15h.01M15 15h.01M10 21v-3h4v3"></path></svg></div><span class="tagline">RBI</span><h3>Banks, NBFCs, payments</h3><p>Cyber-security guidance expects privileged access management, MFA for critical systems and periodic user-access reviews.</p><div class="map"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg><span>PIM \xB7 access reviews \xB7 risk-based MFA</span></div></div>
      <div class="card reg rv" data-d="1"><div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 3v18h18"></path><path d="M7 15l4-4 3 3 5-6"></path></svg></div><span class="tagline">SEBI</span><h3>Market intermediaries</h3><p>The cyber-resilience framework calls for least-privilege access, time-bound admin rights and logged privileged activity.</p><div class="map"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg><span>JIT roles \xB7 approvals \xB7 audit history</span></div></div>
      <div class="card reg rv" data-d="2"><div class="ico o"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path></svg></div><span class="tagline">DPDP Act 2023</span><h3>Every data fiduciary</h3><p>Reasonable security safeguards: limit who can reach personal data, keep audit trails and respond fast to compromise.</p><div class="map"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg><span>Access packages \xB7 expiry \xB7 remediation</span></div></div>
      <div class="card reg rv" data-d="3"><div class="ico r"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 16V11a6 6 0 00-12 0v5l-2 2h16zM10 20a2 2 0 004 0"></path></svg></div><span class="tagline">CERT-In</span><h3>Incident reporting</h3><p>Logs must be kept and incidents reported within six hours \u2014 you need to know about a compromised account quickly.</p><div class="map"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg><span>Risk alerts \xB7 risky sign-in logs</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note-ind rv">P2 supports these requirements; it does not by itself make an organisation compliant. We can map your controls during setup.</p>
  </div>
</section>
