var SUITE_FAQS = [["Do I need Entra ID P1 as well?", "Yes. Every Suite user needs Entra ID P1. It's already included in Microsoft 365 Business Premium, E3, E5, F1/F3 and EMS E3/E5. If your users don't have it, add standalone P1 at \u20B9528 per user per month \u2014 the calculator above can include it."], ["We already have Entra ID P2 or Microsoft 365 E5. Is there a discount?", "Microsoft offers special Suite pricing to existing P2 and E5 customers, since ID Protection is already covered. Contact us with your current licence count and we'll confirm eligibility and quote the difference."], ["Can Private Access fully replace our VPN?", "For most businesses, yes. Start with Quick Access to tunnel the same IP ranges and hostnames your VPN covers, then move to per-app access with separate policies. Private network connectors run on Windows Server and make outbound-only connections over port 443, so nothing is exposed inbound. RDP, SSH, SMB shares, SAP, internal web apps and databases all work."], ["How does Face Check handle personal data?", "The user takes a live selfie that is compared with the photo in a Verified ID credential they hold. The requesting app receives a match result and confidence score, not the selfie itself. Under the DPDP Act you'll still need a clear purpose and notice for using it \u2014 we help you draft both."], ["Can Internet Access run alongside our existing proxy or SSE?", "Yes. It can run side by side with a third-party security service edge, so you can migrate traffic profiles one at a time. Branch connectivity through remote networks needs at least 50 combined P1 and Internet Access licences."], ["Which devices are supported?", "The Global Secure Access client runs on Windows, macOS, iOS and Android. Branch offices can also connect without a client through remote network links."], ["Do I have to licence every employee?", "Licence every user who benefits from a Suite feature. For governance, that includes people whose access is reviewed and the reviewers; for PIM, eligible users and approvers. We'll size it with you so you don't over- or under-buy."], ["What's the difference between monthly and yearly billing?", "Monthly is \u20B9910 per user, billed each month. Yearly is \u20B910,560 per user for 12 months, paid upfront \u2014 cheaper than 12 monthly payments and 12% below Microsoft's list price. Both are excl. 18% GST."], ["Do I get a GST invoice?", "Yes. Every order comes with a GST-compliant invoice from XcellHost Cloud Services Pvt. Ltd. Pay by UPI, card, net banking or bank transfer."]];

